e.0001957-Clark1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>CW</given-names></name><name><surname>Levy</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1988</year><article-title>Diel vertical migrations by juvenile sockeye salmon and the antipredator window.</article-title><source>Am Nat</source><volume>131</volume><fpage>271</fpage><lpage>290</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001957-Jonsson1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jonsson</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Jonsson</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Partial migration: niche shift versus sexual maturation in fishes.</article-title><source>Rev Fish Biol Fish</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>348</fpage><lpage>365</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001957-Schindler1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schindler</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Migration strategies of young fishes under temporal constraints: the effect of size-dependent overwinter mortaility.</article-title><source>Can J Fish Aq Sci</source><volume>56</volume><issue>Suppl 1</issue><fpage>61</fpage><lpage>70</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001957-Tarling1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tarling</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Burrows</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Matthews</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Saboroski</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Buchhoilz</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>An optimisation model of the diel vertical migration of northern krill (<italic>Meganyctiphanes norvegica</italic>) in the Clyde sea and the Kattegat.</article-title><source>Can J Fish Aq Sci</source><volume>57</volume><issue>Suppl 3</issue><fpage>38</fpage><lpage>50</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001957-Borcherding1"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Borcherding</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bauerfeld</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hintzen</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Neumann</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Lateral migrations of fishes between floodplain lakes and their drainage channels at the Lower Rhine: diel and seasonal aspects.</article-title><source>J. Fish Biol.</source><volume>61</volume><fpage>1154</fpage><lpage>1170</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001957-Jobling1"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jobling</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Fish bioenergetics.</article-title><publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Chapman and Hall</publisher-name><fpage>309</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001957-Casselmann1"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Casselmann</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1978</year><article-title>Effects of environmental factors on growth, survival, activity and exploitation of northern pike.</article-title><source>Am Fish Soc Spec Publ</source><volume>11</volume><fpage>114</fpage><lpage>128</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001957-Diana1"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Diana</surname><given-name